{
  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a strong upward trend (e.g., >75 EUR) followed by a model forecast that continues rising linearly, apply a severe mean-reversion correction of -10% to -20% immediately, as true outcomes often crash sharply after such spikes.",
    "If sentiment is neutral (0.00) but the last 3 days show high volatility or a peak, reduce the model's upward forecast slope by 50% and add a downward bias of 1-2 EUR/day to account for overconfidence.",
    "When sentiment shifts from negative (-0.25) to positive (1.00) during a rising trend, do not trust the immediate continuation; instead, cap the first 5 days of forecast at the current price level and assume a 3-5% drop before any recovery.",
    "In volatile regimes where true outcomes oscillate wildly around the model's path, reduce the forecast horizon by half (e.g., use only 10-day trend) and apply a volatility penalty factor of -0.8 to the daily growth rate.",
    "If the last 5 days show a consistent decline in sentiment while prices are rising, reverse the model's upward bias entirely and project a flat or slightly downward trajectory for the next 7 days."
  ]
}
